      opening: "Lymphoedema is swelling caused by a problem with lymph drainage. After cancer treatment, swelling may affect an arm, leg, breast, chest, or another area. The right plan depends on the cancer treatment, surgery, skin condition, infection risk, symptoms, and the advice of the oncology team. It is not safe to treat every new swelling as simple fluid retention.",
      context: "A home plan in Jaipur should fit appointments, heat, clothing, work, family support, and access to the cancer or lymphoedema team. The therapist can help the person practise movement in a familiar setting, but local convenience must not delay a review of new, painful, red, or rapidly increasing swelling.",
